  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner from Melton, Leicestershire, has died following an accident in Jordan on 22 August. Paralysed from the chest down in a 2007 riding accident, she became known for raising nearly £1m through high-profile fundraising events, including completing the 2012 London Marathon over 17 days and the 2016 Great North Run while pregnant, both in a bionic suit. She also lit the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square in 2012. Her family, who described themselves as devastated, have requested privacy to grieve."
